


Next — Check the BIOS drive order using GRUB
Before making changes, run this one read-only command from the live Ubuntu Terminal:
sudo grub-probe --target=device /mnt/ubuntu/boot/grub


If /mnt/ubuntu is not currently mounted, first run:
sudo mkdir -p /mnt/ubuntu
sudo mount -o ro /dev/sda1 /mnt/ubuntu


This helps confirm how GRUB identifies the installed filesystem, but it cannot prove that the BIOS recognizes the hard drive.
